# spark_of_talent — the first magic quest, converted from MagicTutorial.cs
#
# ⚠ DANIEL PAULS' CONVERSATION IS NOT IN THIS FILE — it is quests/dialogue/danielpauls.quest.
# That file owns every line he says, across every quest he appears in: one DIALOGUE block per
# npcId across the whole quests/ tree, because each import regenerates Dialogue_danielpauls.asset
# wholesale and a second declaration would clobber the first. This quest's four Daniel beats (the
# offer, the nudge, the reward, the post-quest farewell) are gated nodes in there.
#
# DIALOGUE underhoused stays HERE deliberately: the geezer appears in this quest and nowhere
# else, which is the case quests/dialogue/ is not for. Move him out the day that stops being true.
#
# ⚠ spark_of_talent is a SAVE KEY. It is the id MagicTutorial has always used and existing saves
# hold it. Never change it.
#
# ⚠ The GRANT: and the COMPLETE: for this quest are both in quests/dialogue/danielpauls.quest.
# Tools -> Content -> Validate Quests only looks for a COMPLETE: inside the quest's own file, so
# it reports this Manual last stage as having no completion route. That is a blind spot in the
# validator, not a hole in the quest.
#
# underhoused's accusations need the ActiveAtStage gate — see
# docs/reference/QUEST_TEXT_FORMAT.md.

QUEST spark_of_talent
TITLE: Serendipity!
GIVER: Daniel Pauls
LOCATION: London, Cellar Entrance.

# Stage 0 — kill the geezer. under_housed is the QuestActor.Key stamped on Enemy_UnderHoused.
STAGE KILL under_housed x1
OBJECTIVE: This jazzy fella wants me to have a word with some oddball. I'll indulge him I guess? He should be just north of where I met Daniel Pauls.

# Stage 1 — MANUAL, not TALKTO, deliberately. A TalkTo final stage completes the quest on the
# interact, BEFORE any choice is picked, which would flip the gates mid-conversation and skip the
# reward beat entirely. The COMPLETE: on Daniel's reward choice, in
# quests/dialogue/danielpauls.quest, is what ends this quest.
STAGE MANUAL
OBJECTIVE: You're crackling with it. Get back to Daniel Pauls and tell him what happened.

# No payout: the reward is Spark itself, taught by the TEACHSPARK choice. A non-zero reward here
# would also retro-pay every existing save that already holds this quest complete.
REWARD
POUNDS: 0
XP: 0

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DIALOGUE underhoused
# Both accusations are gated to stage 0, so once he is dead — and after the quest is over — the
# node has no visible exit and DialogueManager supplies its own escape button. A player who talks
# to him before taking the quest just hears his opening line and leaves.

NODE start
SPEAKER: underhoused
SPEAK: ...You what? I ain't done nothin'. Move along, yeah?
CHOICE Saw you near the Jones' the other night. Bit of a light show, weren't it? -> accuse_lightshow
GATE: stage spark_of_talent 0
CHOICE Someone's been zappin' folk round here. That you, mate? -> accuse_direct
GATE: stage spark_of_talent 0

NODE accuse_lightshow
SPEAKER: underhoused
SPEAK: I don't— I don't know what you're on about. Back off. I'm tellin' you, BACK OFF—

NODE accuse_direct
SPEAKER: underhoused
SPEAK: Nnnh— you shouldn't've said that. You shouldn't've—
